WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:13.549
Hey youtubers, wholock week continues with
my breakdown of how I think sherlock survived

00:00:13.549 --> 00:00:15.170
his fall.

00:00:15.170 --> 00:00:20.130
I promised this the other day but had to postpone
it for some doctor who related stuff yesterday.

00:00:20.130 --> 00:00:23.599
Something about a christmas special, new doctor…

00:00:23.599 --> 00:00:28.490
If you’re just finding me for the first
time this week I’ve been doing a week of

00:00:28.490 --> 00:00:31.010
sherlock and doctor who videos to celebrate
the christmas special and series 3.

00:00:31.010 --> 00:00:32.010
Be sure to subscribe to get everything.

00:00:32.010 --> 00:00:34.900
Normally there’s a much more diverse science
fiction/fantasy fandom offering.

00:00:34.900 --> 00:00:40.540
But special events demand special videos.

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:46.600
So let’s get started.

00:00:46.600 --> 00:00:53.670
Number 1, the ingredients he needed One Molly
Hooper, an undocumented cadaver, a squash

00:00:53.670 --> 00:00:59.100
ball, a network of homeless spies and a well
thought out flight path from the roof to the

00:00:59.100 --> 00:01:00.100
pavement.

00:01:00.100 --> 00:01:05.590
2 - This explanation assumes that it was in
fact sherlock himself that went over the roof

00:01:05.590 --> 00:01:07.300
and not the cadaver.

00:01:07.300 --> 00:01:10.240
3 - Starting from the beginning.

00:01:10.240 --> 00:01:14.190
Sherlock goes to molly and tells her she matters
and that she does in fact count.

00:01:14.190 --> 00:01:16.290
It’s a double meaning though.

00:01:16.290 --> 00:01:17.990
Molly likes to count things.

00:01:17.990 --> 00:01:22.280
But Sherlock finds one extra cadaver in the
morgue.

00:01:22.280 --> 00:01:28.280
4- Sherlock falls from the roof in such a
way to do the least amount of physical damage

00:01:28.280 --> 00:01:29.280
to himself.

00:01:29.280 --> 00:01:34.160
He is injured enough to make it believable
to any passersby that he’s dead.

00:01:34.160 --> 00:01:39.660
5 - Watson’s vision is obscured by a well
timed laundry truck and is knocked to the

00:01:39.660 --> 00:01:43.330
ground by one of sherlock’s homeless spies
on the bicycle.

00:01:43.330 --> 00:01:45.980
Watson never sees sherlock hit the ground.

00:01:45.980 --> 00:01:51.710
6 - Sherlock uses the squash ball to stop
the blood flow at the point where watson takes

00:01:51.710 --> 00:01:53.500
his pulse.

00:01:53.500 --> 00:01:57.220
Not feeling a pulse, Watson in a state of
shock believes sherlock is dead.

00:01:57.220 --> 00:02:00.010
But the body still needs to be examined at
the morgue.

00:02:00.010 --> 00:02:02.860
7 - This is where Molly comes back.

00:02:02.860 --> 00:02:08.220
Sherlock is taken to the morgue still appearing
to be dead and is then revived by Molly wherein

00:02:08.220 --> 00:02:11.190
they switch his body with that of the cadaver.

00:02:11.190 --> 00:02:15.879
They also alter the records so that any officials
investigating will find nothing out of the

00:02:15.879 --> 00:02:16.920
ordinary.

00:02:16.920 --> 00:02:21.750
8 - The Cadaver is buried in sherlock’s
grave.

00:02:21.750 --> 00:02:25.340
9 - What makes this so plausible?

00:02:25.340 --> 00:02:27.200
Irene.

00:02:27.200 --> 00:02:30.420
Remember Irene did the exact same thing in
Scandal.

00:02:30.420 --> 00:02:33.090
Even Sherlock was fooled that she was dead.

00:02:33.090 --> 00:02:37.439
Loving to solve puzzles, she would probably
have explained how she did it much to his

00:02:37.439 --> 00:02:38.749
delight.

00:02:38.749 --> 00:02:41.349
10 - Mycroft.

00:02:41.349 --> 00:02:42.939
Where is mycroft in all this.

00:02:42.939 --> 00:02:46.299
He’s jokingly referred to as the British
Government.

00:02:46.299 --> 00:02:49.460
He knew all about Moriarty long before Sherlock
did.

00:02:49.460 --> 00:02:55.189
Based on this it’s likely that he knows
and is merely impeding any further investigation

00:02:55.189 --> 00:02:56.249
into the matter.

00:02:56.249 --> 00:03:01.269
Which is probably one of the reasons Anderson
lost his job obsessing over it, as we learned

00:03:01.269 --> 00:03:02.989
in the mini episode.

00:03:02.989 --> 00:03:10.780
11 - Why, Moriarty had threatened the lives
of sherlock’s closest friends.

00:03:10.780 --> 00:03:18.219
If he didn’t make his henchmen believe he
was dead, they would still have gone after

00:03:18.219 --> 00:03:19.299
his friends.

00:03:19.299 --> 00:03:21.040
12 - Alternatives.

00:03:21.040 --> 00:03:24.409
There are some who believe that the laundry
truck cushioned sherlock’s fall.

00:03:24.409 --> 00:03:28.709
But both Steven Moffat and Mark Gatiss said
the truck has nothing to do with it.

00:03:28.709 --> 00:03:34.960
All the best theories I’ve seen include
Molly helping sherlock swap bodies and sherlock

00:03:34.960 --> 00:03:35.989
jumping off the roof.

00:03:35.989 --> 00:03:39.430
It’s really the point of impact and the
body bleeding on the pavement that are points

00:03:39.430 --> 00:03:42.109
of contention.

00:03:42.109 --> 00:03:48.420
Let me know what you’re favorite theory
is and remember I’m picking one random subscriber

00:03:48.420 --> 00:03:50.590
from the comments to give a twenty dollar
amazon giftcard to.

00:03:50.590 --> 00:03:52.939
Paypal gift for international viewers.

00:03:52.939 --> 00:03:59.370
I’m working on a bunch more sherlock videos
between now and the premiere.

00:03:59.370 --> 00:04:04.739
Right now you can click here for my breakdown
of the mini episode and here for my top 10

00:04:04.739 --> 00:04:06.700
moments on sherlock so far.

00:04:06.700 --> 00:04:07.889
Thanks for watching.

00:04:07.889 --> 00:04:08.889
High fives.

00:04:08.889 --> 00:04:09.279
see you tomorrow!

